ar outdoor concerts of his music, which feature laser displays and fireworks, and three of which appeared in the Guinness Book of Records for their large audiences.\r\nOne of his albums, Musique pour supermarchés had a print run on only a single copy, which was auctioned to raise money for French artists.\r\nIn 1986 he worked with NASA-Astronaut Ronald McNair was to play the saxophone part of Jarre's piece Rendez-Vous VI while in orbit on board the Space Shuttle Challenger. It was to have been the first piece of music recorded in space, for the album Rendez-Vous.\r\nAfter the Challenger disaster of January 28, 1986, the piece was recorded with a different saxophonist, retitled Ron's piece and the album dedicated to the seven Challenger astronauts.\r\nHe is a UNESCO Goodwill Ambassador and was married to [a=Charlotte Rampling] from 1978 to 1997.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:209415","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":544853,"name":"Jammie Jefferson"},{"id":544857,"name":"1906"},{"id":560038,"name":"Pop Corn Orchestra"},{"id":6904871,"name":"The Foggy Joe Band"}],"groups":[{"active":false,"id":544855,"name":"The Dustbins"},{"active":false,"id":1770847,"name":"Groupe De Recherches Musicales"},{"active":true,"id":2145655,"name":"The Vizitors"}],"members":null,"namevariations":["A. Jarre","Global Dream World/Jean Michael Jarre","I. M. Jarre","J M Jarre","J,M. Jarre","J-M Jarre","J-M. Jarre","J-M. Jarré","J-Michel Jarre","J. Jarre","J. M Jarre","J. M. A. Jarre","J. M. Jarre","J. M. Jarré","J. Maurice Jarre","J. Michel","J. Michel Jarre","J. y M. Jarre","J.-M. Jarre","J.-M. Jarrè","J.Jarre","J.M Jarre","J.M. Farre","J.M. Jarre","J.M.J.","J.M.Jarre","J.M.Jarrei","J.Michel Jarre","JM Jarre","JM Jarre (JMJ Associes Eternity)","JM. Jarre","JMJ","JML","Jarre","Jarre J M","Jarre, J.M.","Jarre, Jean Michel André","Jarre, Jean-Michel","Jarre, Jean-Michel Andre","Jarremix","Jarrie","Jean - Michel Jarre","Jean M. Jarre","Jean Michael Jaree","Jean Michael Jarre","Jean Michae